## Controllers

**paymentController.js** — imports `paymentFileService` (as `paymentService`), `paymentReadinessService`, `hrmsSyncService`, `auditService`. Endpoints: `eligiblePeriods`, `preview` (calls `readinessService.preview(req.query.payPeriodId)`, on error records `auditService.record({action:"PAYMENT_READINESS_FAILURE", entityType:"pay_period", entityId:req.query.payPeriodId, details:{errorCode}})`), `generate` (calls `paymentFileService.generate({payPeriodId: req.body.payPeriodId, user, ipAddress})`), `list`, `getById`, `download` (streams CSV, sets `Content-Disposition`), `retryHrms` (calls `hrmsSyncService.retry`), `cancel` (calls `paymentFileService.cancel({batchId, reason: req.body.reason, user, ipAddress})`), `statistics`.

**payslipController.js** — imports `payslipService`. Endpoints: `listForBatch`, `listMine`, `listAll`, `getById` (returns `payslipService.serialize(payslip)`), `download` (streams PDF via `createPdfDownload`, `Content-Type: application/pdf`).

## Services

**paymentReadinessService.js** — `classifyBankDetails(staff)`: missing (`!staff.bank_code` or `!staff.bank_account_no`) → status `"missing"`; format regex mismatch → `"invalid"`; else `"ready"`. `assess(payPeriodId, transaction, {allowBankIssues=false})` throws `PAY_PERIOD_NOT_FOUND`, `DUPLICATE_PAYMENT_BATCH` (existing non-cancelled batch), `PERIOD_NOT_APPROVED` (`payPeriod.status !== "approved"`), `PERIOD_NOT_LOCKED` (`!payPeriod.is_locked`), `APPROVAL_RECORD_MISSING`, `PAYROLL_LINES_MISSING`, `INCOMPLETE_PAYROLL_LINE` (`line.status !== "ok"`), and — **only when `allowBankIssues` is false** — `MISSING_BANK_DETAILS` / `INVALID_BANK_DETAILS`. `paymentFileService.generate()` calls `readinessService.assess(payPeriodId, transaction)` with the default `allowBankIssues=false`, meaning **actual batch generation blocks entirely and creates NO `payment_batch_item` rows if any staff has missing/invalid bank details** — payment_batch_items are only ever built afterward from `readiness.payrollLines`, which by that point is guaranteed 100% bank-clean. `allowBankIssues: true` is used only by `preview()`, which never writes to the DB. (This resolves the apparent contradiction with the seed data's NULL bank rows: those items were inserted directly via seed SQL for demo purposes, not through the generate() code path, which is consistent with `bank_code`/`bank_account_no` being nullable columns even though real generate() runs never populate NULLs.)

**paymentFileService.js** — `generate()`: wraps in `sequelize.transaction({isolationLevel:"SERIALIZABLE"})`; creates `PaymentBatch` with `batch_reference: generateReference("PAY")` (format `PAY-<timestamp>-<hex>`, confirmed by seed data e.g. `PAY-20260722143603-F562F5`), `file_format:"giro"`, `status:"generated"`, `hrms_sync_status:"not_started"`, `generated_by:user.id`, `generated_at:new Date()`; bulk-creates `PaymentBatchItem` rows with `payment_reference: \`${batch_reference}-${staff.external_ref}\``. After transaction, records `PAYMENT_BATCH_GENERATED` audit then immediately calls `hrmsSyncService.sync()`. `cancel()`: only allowed when `batch.status` in `["generated","hrms_sync_failed"]`, else `INVALID_CANCELLATION`; sets `status:"cancelled", cancelled_by:user.id, cancelled_at:new Date(), cancellation_reason:reason`; also resets `PayPeriod.status` back to `"approved"` if it wasn't `"payment_ready"`. No `file_path` used anywhere; CSV generated in-memory via `generateGiroCsv` (utils/giroFileFormatter) and returned directly for `/download` and inline in `getById` (only metadata: fileName/mimeType/sizeBytes/checksumSha256).

**hrmsSyncService.js** — `sync()`: rejects if `status==="cancelled"`; no-op returns batch if `status==="completed"`. On retry, audits `HRMS_RETRY`. Sets `status:"hrms_sync_pending", hrms_sync_status:"pending"`, audits `HRMS_SYNC_START`. Calls `hrmsAdapter.sync(payload)`. On failure: `status:"hrms_sync_failed", hrms_sync_status:"failed", hrms_error_message`, audits `HRMS_SYNC_FAILURE`, throws `AppError(502,"HRMS_SYNC_FAILURE",...)`. On success (in a transaction): `status:"completed", hrms_sync_status:"completed", hrms_reference:result.externalReference, hrms_error_message:null, hrms_synced_at:new Date()`; also sets `PayPeriod.status = "payment_ready"`; then calls `payslipService.generateForBatch({batchId, transaction})` — **this is exactly what triggers payslip generation, only on successful HRMS sync completion**, and audits `HRMS_SYNC_SUCCESS` then `PAYSLIP_GENERATION` per payslip. `retry()` only allowed when `status==="hrms_sync_failed"`, else `INVALID_HRMS_RETRY`.

**payslipService.js** — `generateForBatch`: builds `payslip_reference: \`PS-${batch.batch_reference}-${item.id.slice(0,8)}\`.slice(0,60)`, `company_name: process.env.COMPANY_NAME || "Emergencies First Aid & Rescue"`, copies `pay_period_start/end` from `batch.payPeriod`, and all money fields from the `payment_batch_item`. Uses `Payslip.bulkCreate(records, {transaction, ignoreDuplicates:true})` — idempotent re-sync safe. PDF is generated on the fly via `pdfkit` in `createPdf()`/`createPdfDownload()`; never persisted as bytes in DB or disk. `assertAccess`: managers see all; employees only their own (`user.staffId === payslip.staff_id`), else `403 PAYSLIP_ACCESS_DENIED`.

## Routes
`payments.js`: manager-only (`authorize("manager")`), routes `/eligible-periods`, `/preview`, `/dashboard/statistics`, `POST /generate` (body `payPeriodId`), `GET /`, `GET /:batchId`, `GET /:batchId/file`, `GET /:batchId/payslips`, `POST /:batchId/retry-hrms`, `PATCH /:batchId/cancel` (body `reason`).
`payslips.js`: authenticated; `/me` (own), `/` (manager `listAll`), `/:payslipId`, `/:payslipId/pdf`.

## Migrations (verbatim, full)

**20260720000100-user-account.js**: creates `user_account` table exactly as model fields plus `created_at`/`updated_at`; adds CHECK constraints `user_account_role_check` (`role IN ('manager','employee')`) and `user_account_status_check` (`status IN ('active','disabled')`). `role`/`status` stored as plain `STRING(20)`, not native ENUM, in the DB (checked via CHECK constraint instead).

**20260720000110-pay-period-is-locked.js**: conditionally `addColumn("pay_period","is_locked", {BOOLEAN, allowNull:false, defaultValue:false})` and `addColumn("pay_period","locked_at",{DATE, allowNull:true})`.

**20260720000120-payment-batch-columns.js**: conditionally adds `batch_reference` (STRING(50), NOT NULL, unique), `employee_count` (INTEGER, NOT NULL, default 0), `total_amount` (DECIMAL(14,2), NOT NULL, default 0), `hrms_sync_status` (STRING(20), NOT NULL, default `"not_started"`, with CHECK `hrms_sync_status IN (...)`), `hrms_reference` (STRING(100), nullable), `hrms_error_message` (STRING(500), nullable), `generated_by` (UUID, NOT NULL, FK → `user_account.id`), `hrms_synced_at` (DATE, nullable), `cancelled_by` (UUID, nullable, FK → `user_account.id`), `cancelled_at` (DATE, nullable), `cancellation_reason` (STRING(500), nullable). Also drops and recreates the `payment_batch_status_check` CHECK constraint to include `generating`/`cancelled` (full list: `generating, generated, hrms_sync_pending, hrms_sync_failed, completed, cancelled`).

**20260720000130-payment-batch-item.js** (full, re-confirmed): creates table if not exists with columns: `id` UUID PK default `uuid_generate_v4()`; `payment_batch_id` UUID NOT NULL FK→`payment_batch.id`; `payroll_line_id` UUID NOT NULL FK→`payroll_line.id`; `staff_id` UUID NOT NULL FK→`staff.id`; `employee_reference` STRING(100) NOT NULL; `employee_name` STRING(150) NOT NULL; **`bank_code` STRING(20) allowNull:true**; **`bank_account_no` STRING(100) allowNull:true**; `gross_pay/incentive_pay/cpf_amount/sdl_amount` DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL; `other_deduction` DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL default 0; `net_pay` DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL; `payment_reference` STRING(100) NOT NULL; `created_at`/`updated_at` DATE NOT NULL default NOW(). Adds indexes on `payment_batch_id` and `staff_id`. No unique constraint on `payment_reference` despite being reference-like. **Confirms the model's `allowNull:false` for bank_code/bank_account_no is wrong; the actual DB schema (and seed data) has them nullable.**

**20260720000140-payslip.js** (full, re-confirmed): creates table if not exists with `id` UUID PK default `uuid_generate_v4()`; `payment_batch_id`/`payroll_line_id`/`staff_id` UUID NOT NULL with FKs to `payment_batch.id`/`payroll_line.id`/`staff.id` respectively; `payslip_reference` STRING(60) NOT NULL unique; `company_name` STRING(150) NOT NULL; `employee_reference` STRING(100) NOT NULL; `employee_name` STRING(150) NOT NULL; `pay_period_start`/`pay_period_end` DATEONLY NOT NULL; `gross_pay/incentive_pay/cpf_amount/sdl_amount` DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL; `other_deduction` DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL default 0; `net_pay` DECIMAL(12,2) NOT NULL; `batch_reference` STRING(50) NOT NULL (no unique — many payslips share one batch_reference); `generated_at` DATE NOT NULL default NOW(); `created_at`/`updated_at` DATE NOT NULL default NOW(). Adds indexes on `payment_batch_id` and `staff_id`.

